int)'","pyproject.toml:151 `pricing = [\"genai-prices\"]` and pyproject.toml:160 `evals = [\"genai-prices\"]` — two extras naming the identical single dependency","The plan text intends REUSE of `pricing`, but the mechanism creates a second, parallel extra rather than composing/referencing the first"],"finding":"The plan introduces a new `evals` pyproject extra whose only content duplicates the existing `pricing` extra (both are just `genai-prices`), while the plan's own Scope line says 'the pricing extra becomes a dependency of the eval package's entry point' — a config-surface duplication where the two extras can silently drift.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f268e750640c1c8f1","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope section — pyproject.toml line; `pyproject.toml` evals/pricing extras","norm_id":"n6476873bb3333129","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["genai-prices is version-pinned or renamed in the `pricing` extra but the `evals` extra is forgotten, so eval installs silently get a divergent pricing dependency","A reader reconciling the Scope's 'pricing extra becomes a dependency' wording against a distinct `evals` extra cannot tell which is authoritative"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Make the eval entry point depend on the existing `pricing` extra (e.g. via a self-referential `nava-rebar[pricing]` in the `evals` extra) so `genai-prices` is declared in exactly one place, matching the plan's stated intent.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respect