rices ... pre-flights a cost estimate and refuses ... $200 total with a $30 reserve') matches the leaf exactly — the leaf is a subset of the EPIC, not of the Tier-0 story"],"finding":"The leaf's declared scope is not a subset of its declared parent (the Tier-0 Pass-3 replay story). The parent's plan and ACs are exclusively about Pass-3 verdict replay (tier0.py, report.py, verdict-flip/friction/per-criterion metrics); the leaf delivers an entirely different deliverable — the eval budget ledger (ledger.py, ledger.jsonl, $200 cap, pre-flight estimate, genai-prices finalization, reconcile) — which appears nowhere in the parent's contract. The leaf itself names the Tier-0 ticket as a peer consumer of its output, and the grandparent epic lists Tier-0 and the ledger as separate children, confirming the ledger belongs to the epic's child-6 (ledger + model-parity + Bedrock chain), not to the Tier-0 story.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faaa9b5cfbe43c98d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Whole ticket vs declared parent 5d19-52e0-7c26-47fb (bouncy-peacockish-titmouse); Scope section and 'python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay CLI' paragraph","norm_id":"nbf7fad20fdd16e6e","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewing whether the ledger leaf's contract is contained by its declared parent's plan","A reader following parent->child links expects Tier-0 (Pass-3 replay) work but finds budget-ledger work"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Change parent_id from the Tier-0 story (5d19-52e0-7c26-47fb / bouncy-peacockish-titmouse) to the epic (759e-7dc1-675c-4877), whose invariant-1 budget/ledger scope and child-6 decomposition already contain this leaf as consistent narrowing.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current